The Go rendering: one command module whose command calls one function of a
package, beside two dead exported functions of that package that each call an
unexported function nothing else calls. An inline directive withholds the first.
Nothing in the module imports anything outside it, so the rendering loads with no
network access.

-- fixture.json --
{
  "symbols": {
    "Live": { "file": "target/ledger/ledger.go", "line": 4 },
    "Withheld": { "file": "target/ledger/ledger.go", "line": 9 },
    "balance": { "file": "target/ledger/ledger.go", "line": 12 },
    "Reported": { "file": "target/ledger/ledger.go", "line": 15 },
    "audit": { "file": "target/ledger/ledger.go", "line": 18 }
  }
}
-- target/go.mod --
module example.com/target

go 1.27.0
-- target/main.go --
package main

import "example.com/target/ledger"

func main() { println(ledger.Live()) }
-- target/ledger/ledger.go --
package ledger

// Live is called by the command.
func Live() int { return 1 }

// Withheld is exported and called by nothing; the directive withholds it.
//
//deadset:ignore DS1001 -- Kept for a caller outside the module.
func Withheld() int { return balance() }

// balance is called by Withheld alone, so it falls with it.
func balance() int { return 2 }

// Reported is exported and called by nothing.
func Reported() int { return audit() }

// audit is called by Reported alone, so it falls with it.
func audit() int { return 3 }
